# The image serves the application; it does not run the experiments.
# benchmarks/ alone is ~15 MB of corpora and result CSVs that nothing at
# runtime reads -- verified by grep: no module outside benchmarks/ and tools/
# refers to that directory except in comments.
benchmarks/
tests/

.git/
.gitignore
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Never let a local .env into an image: it carries the service role key, which
# bypasses row-level security.  Secrets come from the Space's own settings.
.env
.env.local
.afc_secret

# Local development artefacts.
afc_app.sqlite3*
afc_results/
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Built here by the RUN step above; a host-built copy would be the wrong
# architecture.
*.so
*.stale

# The committed Windows build.  On Linux the loader tries it first, fails with
# "invalid ELF header", and falls through to the .so -- harmless, but it puts a
# spurious failure line in the diagnostics the Settings page shows.
*.dll

# Documentation and changelogs are not needed at runtime.  README.md is kept:
# Spaces reads its YAML frontmatter to configure the Space.
CHANGES*.md
DEAD_WEIGHT_PROPOSAL.md
NATIVE_WINDOWS_X64.md
SCOPE_NOTES.md
SIZE_POLICY.md
DEPLOYMENT.md
